		{"id":"uncertainty","type":"text","x":0,"y":609,"width":460,"height":154,"color":"2","text":"### Uncertainty\n\n- Child findings may not transfer to adults\n- Support outcomes reflect who chose them\n- Risk genes do not determine traits"},
		{"id":"hypothesis","type":"text","x":0,"y":823,"width":460,"height":232,"color":"6","text":"### Open questions\n\n- Which outcomes do autistic people themselves prioritise, and how are they measured?\n- How do rare and common variation combine in individual developmental trajectories?\n- Which adult service models have measured effects, in which systems, and on which outcomes?"},
		{"id":"evidence-basis","type":"text","x":0,"y":1115,"width":460,"height":249,"color":"4","text":"### Evidence basis\n\nP31949163: abstract-only, abstract_checked\nF20: official-pdf, educational_checked\nP24808851: open-access-online, full_text_checked\nP31981491: abstract-only, abstract_checked\nF24: official-page, educational_checked\nP42411151: open-access-online, full_text_checked\nP41993846: open-access-online, full_text_checked"}
